English Translation:
..... In the ARSENAL of the VENETIANS,
In winter, the tenacious pitch boils
To re-pitch their unsound vessels,
For they cannot sail; and instead,
Some make their new vessel, and some patch up
The sides of that which has made the most voyages;
Some re-hammer from bow and some from stern;
Others make oars, and others coil rigging;
Some patch the foresail and mizzen-sail;
INFERNO CANTO XXI, VERSES VII-XV

Italian Translation:
….. NELL’ARZANÀ DE’ VINIZIANI
BOLLE L’INVERNO LA TENACE PECE
A RIMPALMAR LI LEGNI LOR NON S.I,
CHÉ NAVIGAR NON PONNO, E IN QUELLA VECE
CHI FA IL SUO LEGNO NUOVO, E CHI RISTOPPA
LE COSTE A QUEL CHE PIÙ VIAGGI FECE;
CHI RIBATTE DA PRODA E CHI DA POPPA;
ALTRI FA REMI, ED ALTRI VOLGE SARTE:
CHI TERZERUOLO ED ARTIMON RINTOPPA;
INF.C. XXI VERSI VII-XV
